From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan <ryan@esterlines.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 14:58:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Build Ladybird with xenon-ublock's engine patches

xenon-ublock carries a Ladybird patch series that adds what uBlock
Origin needs beyond Ladybird's content blocker: scriptlets, procedural
and action cosmetic filters, $redirect surrogates, $removeparam, $popup
and $method filters, CNAME uncloaking, and an element picker.

Meta/xenon.py applies the series with xenon-ublock's engine/apply.py
into Build/ladybird-patched, a copy of the ladybird submodule (which
stays as it is), and builds that. The copy is only redone when the
submodule or the patches change. xenon-ublock is found through
XENON_UBLOCK_DIR, ./xenon-ublock or ../xenon-ublock.

Meta/update-filter-lists.py now converts the lists for the patched
engine, so they keep uBlock Origin's scriptlets and the other filters
the stock engine drops. uBlock Origin's own lists go in trusted-lists/,
which UI/FilterLists.cpp passes as --trusted-content-blocker-list so
they may use the scriptlets uBO reserves for its lists, and uBO's
scriptlets and redirect surrogates go in resources/, passed as
--content-blocker-resources. Meta/check.py knows the new layout.

The context menu's new Block Element... action (from the patches) ends
in a dialog that shows the picked element's filter for the user to edit
and add to the custom filters (UI/ElementPicker.cpp).
